  INDEN file: cu63e81b2_PopWe2TotIn6RB                            2925 1451
  Cu-63 evaluation developed within the INDEN collaboration       2925 1451
  M.Pigni and J.McDonnell(ORNL), A.Trkov(JSI), R.Capote(IAEA)     2925 1451
  M. Kostal (CVR, Rez, CZ), Y. Danon(RPI)                         2925 1451
------------------------------------------------------------------2925 1451
Resonance parameters from ORNL by J.McDonnell,M.Pigni (25/01/2024)2925 1451
- Elast.ang.dist. in the RRR by Popov86                           2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
Cu-63 List of changes by A. Trkov, R. Capote, January 2024        2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
The changes were made to match the neutron emission spectrum      2925 1451
at 14.1 MeV measured by Takahashi and to improve the performance  2925 1451
in modelling the Rez Cu cube transmission benchmark. The          2925 1451
performance in criticality benchmarks is largely unaffected.      2925 1451
The reactivity of the IMF020 cases is slightly over-predicted,    2925 1451
but we suspect there is a bias in the benchmark since IMF021      2925 1451
that contains no copper is similarly over-predicted (+200pcm).    2925 1451
- Elast.ang.dist. 100-300 keV by Popov86, 0.3-1.2 MeV Smith64     2925 1451
- Reduced elastic cross section in the range 0.1-1 MeV by 1pc.    2925 1451
- Insert Weigand data for capture, reduced by 5 percent (also RRR)2925 1451
- Replace MF6/MT91 by JENDL-4.0 above 7 MeV.                      2925 1451
- Replace discrete and continuum inelastic cross sections by      2925 1451
  JENDL-4.0/HE above 6 MeV; apply ad-hoc corrections to ensure    2925 1451
  smooth transition.                                              2925 1451
- Replace (n,np) cross sections with JENDL-4.0/HE.                2925 1451
- Replace total cross section from JENDL-4.0/HE above 2.7 MeV     2925 1451
  because it agrees with Finlay data; adjust elastic              2925 1451
  for consistency.                                                2925 1451
- Increase the total by up to 0.7 pc in the range 5-6 MeV to      2925 1451
  improve the agreement with Finlay data.                         2925 1451
- Cu-63(n,a), Cu63(n,2n) and Cu65(n,2n) from IRDFF-II             2925 1451
- ALARM-CF-CU-SHIELD-001-FINAL shielding benchmark (Rez,CZ)       2925 1451
- M.Schulc+ Nucl. Eng. Technol. 53, 3151 (2021).                  2925 1451
- Quasidifferential RPI exp. Nucl. Sci. Eng. 196, 121 (2022).     2925 1451
***************************************************************** 2925 1451
Cu-63 List of changes since the release of ENDF/B-VIII.1_beta-2   2925 1451
  Updates of energy-angular distributions related to the emitted  2925 1451
  charged particles ( AUG. 2023)                                  2925 1451
  H.I. Kim (KAERI),                                               2925 1451
  H.Y. Lee, T. Kawano, S.A. Kuvin, and M.W. Herman (LANL)         2925 1451
  Energy-angular distributions of discrete and continuum levels   2925 1451
  and photon transitions related to emitted charged particles     2925 1451
  (proton, deuteron, triton, helium-3 and alpha)                  2925 1451
  have been updated [1] using CoH3 [2] and formatted into         2925 1451
  the ENDF-6 format using DeCE [3]. The Q-values have been        2925 1451
  calculated using the mass data in Audi's 2012 mass table [4]    2925 1451
  and FRDM2012 massess [5].                                       2925 1451
  Summary of updated MF/MT                                        2925 1451
  MF=6  MT= 103, 104, 105, 107 were deleted.                      2925 1451
  MF=3  MT= 600-609, 649, 650-659, 699, 700-709, 749, 800-809,    2925 1451
            849 were added.                                       2925 1451
  MF=6  MT= 600-609, 649, 650-659, 699, 700-709, 749, 800-809,    2925 1451
            849 were added.                                       2925 1451
References:                                                       2925 1451
[1] H.I.Kim et al., Nucl. Instr. Method A 963, 163699 (2020)      2925 1451
[2] T.Kawano, Springer Proceedings in Physics 254, pp.27  (2021)  2925 1451
[3] T.Kawano, J. Nucl. Sci. Technol. 56, (11) 1029 (2019)         2925 1451
[4] G.Audi et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 120, 1 (2014)                2925 1451
[5] P.Moller et al., At. Data and Nucl. Data Tables 109, 1 (2012) 2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451 
**************************** ENDF/B-VII.1 ************************2925 1451
Trial version by combining ORNL resonance parameters and LANL     2925 1451
high energy part. The resolved resonance range was lowered to     2925 1451
100 keV, and the LANL evaluation was extended to that energy.     2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
                                        T. Kawano (Aug. 16, 2016) 2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
