Resonance Parameter and Angular Distribution Information          2925 1451
-------------------------------                                   2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
 29-Cu- 63 ORNL, MIT Resonance Evaluation Including Covariance    2925 1451
 and Angular Distribution of Elastic Scattering                   2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
 V. Sobes, L. C. Leal, K. Guber, G. Arbanas and D. Wiarda         2925 1451
 B. Forget                                                        2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
Resolved resonance parameter evaluation for Cu-63 was done with   2925 1451
the computer code SAMMY.[ref1]  The following data were used in   2925 1451
the SAMMY analysis.                                               2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
     Reference      |   Energy (eV)     | Facility | Measurement  2925 1451
--------------------|-------------------|----------|------------  2925 1451
Pandey et al.[ref2] |    32 - 185 000   | ORELA    | Trans.  78m  2925 1451
Pandey et al.[ref2] | 1 000 - 1 400 000 | ORELA    | Trans.  78m  2925 1451
Guber et al.[ref3]  |   100 - 90 000    | GELINA   | Capt.   58m  2925 1451
Guber et al.[ref3]  |   100 - 300 000   | GELINA   | Capt.   58m  2925 1451
Sobes et al.[ref4]  |  0.01 - 0.1       | MITR     | Trans.  1.2m 2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
The MITR transmission measurements were important for determining 2925 1451
the shape and the uncertainty of the thermal cross section.       2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
A set of resonance parameter describing the experimental data     2925 1451
was obtained. Resonance parameter covariance matrices were also   2925 1451
obtained in the SAMMY evaluation process. The upper energy        2925 1451
boundary of the resonance region of Cu-63 was extended from       2925 1451
99.5 keV to 300 keV.                                              2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
Thermal cross section obtained in the present evaluation are      2925 1451
compared to the values listed in the Atlas of Neutron Resonances  2925 1451
in the following table:                                           2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
    Cross Section        ORNL                  Atlas              2925 1451
       Capt          4.471+/-0.13           4.50+/-0.02           2925 1451
       Total         9.573+/-0.10           9.60+/-0.20           2925 1451
       Scat          5.102+/-0.15            5.1+/-0.2            2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
 Capture Res. Int.   4.938+/-0.23           4.97+/-0.08           2925 1451
 Energy Limits      0.5 eV - 300 keV      0.5 eV - 20.0 MeV       2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
Angular distribution data for elastic scattering for incident     2925 1451
neutron energies between 1e-5 eV and 300 keV were generated       2925 1451
directely from the new resonance parameters in File 2 on a fine   2925 1451
energy grid. The new elastic scattering angular distribution      2925 1451
data gives a much more detailed treatment of the angular          2925 1451
distribution than previous evaluations.                           2925 1451
                                                                  2925 1451
